-- Tabletop Simulator adapter for the Battlegrounds engine (v4: Codex's Tabletop Arena boards).
-- Runs on the hidden "Battlegrounds Tavern" controller object. All game state lives here.
--  * Idle table: only the Tabletop Arena Setup Box ("Play Hearthstone Battlegrounds"). Its button
--    opens a settings panel on the table beside it (season, timer, Buddies, Trinkets, Anomalies, Start).
--  * v4.1: no XML/HUD at all. Controls (Tier Up, Refresh, Freeze, Hero Power, End Turn, gold, hero Health)
--    are tokens with the user's BG_Assets art and invisible buttons; Discover choices lie below the board.
--  * Every image is loaded from the user's GitHub (Jnipko488/mtg-table-data, hsbg/), pinned to a commit.
--  * Each player gets a copy of Codex's "Tabletop Arena" board, driven with setArenaPhase.
--  * Game start: 4 heroes per player on their board; hover one to see its Hero Power.
--  * Minions are real Hearthstone card renders with the stat numbers erased from the gems; TTS
--    draws live Attack/Health on the gems and keyword art (BG_Assets) on the card.
--  * Drag a tavern card into your hand (or onto your board) to buy it, drop a hand card on the
--    board to play it, drag a warband card back up to the tavern / Bob to sell it.
